Changes
    The objects are too intelligent and contain too much knowledge of their surroundings.
    True cells cannot see and store sight data like food direction.
    Cells will literally bump into each other and eat each other if their diet includes meat. But they don't hunt.
    cells have orientation  so I will need to implement such a thing.

    SO I might be able to get away with creating a basic pathfinding evolution finder. Basically pre program basic behaviors
    like turning and spinning and allow the cell to create it's own algorthithm/movement behavior.

    every cell or object has a Vector2D object that will determine it's movement vector. it does not contain any data in regards to it's location.
    That's stored in the environment object and is used for rendering, and collisions where a check is performed to see if any two objects occupy the same space.
    this check is performed by a stack that is created every tick, as objects are added to the stack for occupied spaces, if two objects are found to occupy
    the same space, one of the objects is eliminated and a state is triggered within the surviving object.
    The direction that the object is facing is determined by finding the angle of magnitude (not sure of correct term) by comparing the x and y velocities.